    "body": "Hmm, the behavior in Chromium is that `dialog0` is left showing as a popover. And that's what I'd expect, I guess, right? Removing the `open` attribute on the modal dialog closes it, and it's free to be re-opened as a popover.\r\n\r\n(This is precisely why I really didn't want to add an `open` attribute for popovers.)",
