    "created_at": "2023-05-26T18:55:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-26T18:55:25Z",
    "body": "> This isn't the case per the spec right now, the modal dialog will be hidden (display: none), but still in the top layer.\r\n\r\nBoo. That's the case also in Chromium, but it is rendered `display:none`. However, the popover behavior does seem to still work correctly I think. There could be some issues behind the scenes.\r\n\r\nI wonder if we shouldn't change the spec so that removing `open` closes the dialog and explicitly removes from the top layer?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
